<title>UK: Czarnikow sees higher Guatemala 1997 sugar offtake.</title>
<headline>Czarnikow sees higher Guatemala 1997 sugar offtake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar consumption in Guatemala could reach some 445,000 tonnes raw value in 1997, up from the previous estimate of 430,000 tonnes, Czarnikow Sugar said in its latest report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In per capita terms this is quite high at 40 kilos raw value and although the long-term rise in overall consumption has been mainly driven by population growth, economic conditions ahev also assisted more recently.&quot;</p>
<p>According to Czarnikow data, Guatemala's sugar consumption is the second highest in the central American and Caribbean region after Cuba.</p>
<p>Estimated consumption reached 425,000 tonnes in 1996.</p>
<p>More than 75 percent of sugar usage in Guatemala was direct consumption although the remaining share of industrial usage had the potential to pick up as the economy improved, Carnikow said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
